title: Reading a visual novel
intro: Save slots with screenshots, a log of the lines said, Skip through what you've read, and Auto.
project: Empty | Reading Story

chapter: The reading menus | Entity > Genres > Visual Novels > Stage
create: Stage
expectcount: Reading Menus = 1
expectcount: Quick Menu = 1
expectcount: Save Screen = 1
expectcount: Load Screen = 1
expectcount: Log Screen = 1
say: A new stage comes with its reading menus: a row of buttons at the top of the screen, save and load screens, a log, and settings.
select: Slot 1
explain: component:SaveSlot | Save Slot | Each card on the save screen is a button that saves in its slot, and a Save Slot that shows the game saved there: a screenshot, when, and the line being said.
select: Lines
explain: component:Backlog | Backlog | The log keeps every line said, with who said it, and the choices picked.

chapter: Skip and Auto | Ctrl skips, A reads on by itself
play
wait: 2
expectvalue: Stage.Dialogue.Line = 1
say: First a quick save, then read on a few lines.
gameclick: Q.Save
wait: 1
gameclick: 0, 3
wait: 2
gameclick: 0, 3
wait: 2
gameclick: 0, 3
wait: 2
expectvalue: Stage.Dialogue.Line = 4
gameclick: Q.Load
wait: 1.5
expectvalue: Stage.Dialogue.Line = 1
explain: game | Quick load | Quick load goes back to the quick save: the stage, the talk and the flags exactly as they were.
say: Hold Control and the lines read before go by in a moment, stopping at the first line not read yet.
hold: LeftControl 1.5
wait: 0.5
expectvalue: Stage.Dialogue.Line = 5
say: A turns on Auto: once a line has typed out, the next comes after a pause as long as the line. It waits at choices.
tap: A
wait: 6
expectvalue: Stage.Dialogue.Line = 6
tap: A
tap: D2
wait: 2
expectvalue: Stage.Stage.Background = Room

chapter: Save slots and the log | Save, Load and the mouse wheel
gameclick: Save
wait: 1
gameclick: -5.2, 1.5
wait: 1
expectvalue: Slot 1.SaveSlot.HasSave = true
explain: game | Saved in slot 1 | The card shows a screenshot of the game without the menu, when it was saved, and the line being said.
tap: Escape
wait: 0.5
gameclick: 0, 3
wait: 2
gameclick: Load
wait: 1
gameclick: -5.2, 1.5
wait: 1.5
expectvalue: Stage.Dialogue.Line = 13
say: Loading slot 1 puts it all back. Saved games are kept for next time, on the desktop and in a browser.
wheel: game = up
wait: 1
expectvalue: Log Screen.Panel.Open = true
explain: game | The log | Turning the mouse wheel up opens the log of what was said. Scroll it with the wheel, the arrow keys, or a finger, and turn the wheel down past the end to close it.
tap: Escape
stop
say: That's reading a visual novel: save slots with screenshots, quick saves, a log of the lines said, Skip for what you've read, and Auto.
